  "notes": "Draft condition, heads, thresholds, J passes, refresh and chain policy are the fast6 J1-R1 recipe unchanged. Candidate bytes use a same-host Linux Unix socket with main-thread intake and no reader thread or spin. Full outcome taps are prepared during target forward; after host acceptance the unchanged packet is delivered through symmetric peer memory and its pinned command mailbox. Prefill/exit keep TCP boundaries; reverse command socket and NCCL no-ACK outcomes are off while peer delivery is on. Keep: CANDIDATE_DECODE_LEAN, wire ring, chain prepost and ordered command counter. Drop: VERIFY_SELECT_LEAN and SELECT_HOST; all device target staging, early plan/reuse/blob/input, fused outcome, presync pack and late/post-lean knobs. Reference target uses causal N=1 FlashInfer graph capture/replay, graph-var zeroing, a plan every round and utils.verify.verify with its upstream syncs. AR steps fail closed.",
